        <div class="takeaways">
          <h3>Key Takeaways</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>For maximum water savings and high-value crops,</strong> Drip irrigation is the clear winner, despite higher upfront costs that are heavily subsidized.</li>
            <li><strong>For field crops on uneven terrain,</strong> Sprinklers offer a pragmatic middle ground.</li>
            <li><strong>Flood irrigation is the baseline “villain”</strong> of India’s water crisis and should be phased out where possible.</li>
            <li><strong>Farm ponds are a complementary strategy,</strong> not a replacement for efficient application methods, especially in Maharashtra’s drought-prone zones.</li>
          </ul>
